WHAT THIS REPOSITORY CONTAINS
=============================

Build scripts only. No upstream source is vendored here. Each script clones its
upstream at build time, applies its patches, and builds -- so what this
repository holds is the *diff*, not the code being patched.


WHY AGPL-3.0
============

A patch is a derivative of the file it modifies and carries that file's licence.
This repository patches works under several licences at once, so the repository
as a whole is distributed under the strongest of them -- Terracotta's AGPL-3.0.

    Script                    Upstream                Upstream licence
    ------------------------  ----------------------  -------------------
    build-mobileglues.sh      MobileGlues             LGPL-2.1-only
    build-terracotta.sh       Terracotta-lib          AGPL-3.0
                              EasyTier                LGPL-3.0
    build-javaapp.sh          Amethyst-iOS            GPL-3.0
                              LWJGL                   BSD-3-Clause
    build-lwjgl-natives.sh    LWJGL                   BSD-3-Clause
                              libffi                  MIT
    build-spirv-cross.sh      SPIRV-Cross             Apache-2.0
    build-sdl3.sh             SDL                     Zlib
    build-shaderc.sh          shaderc                 Apache-2.0
                              glslang                 BSD-3-Clause and others
                              SPIRV-Tools             Apache-2.0

If you want a single patch on its own terms, the patch to a MobileGlues file is
equally available to you under LGPL-2.1-only, and the patch to an Amethyst-iOS
file under GPL-3.0 -- each matching the file it modifies. AGPL-3.0 applies to
the collection.


build-shaderc.sh builds its upstreams without modifying them; glslang and
SPIRV-Tools come in through shaderc's own pinned dependency set.


WHERE TO FIND THINGS
====================

    patches/     The complete diff each script produces, as readable unified
                 diffs. This is the "modified module" in the form that matters:
                 vendoring the patched upstream trees whole would be hundreds of
                 megabytes, most of it unchanged. Regenerate with
                 EMIT_PATCH_DIR=<dir> ./Scripts/build-<name>.sh

    licenses/    The full licence text of every upstream this repository
                 patches, copied verbatim from each project.

    Scripts/     The build scripts themselves. CI runs exactly these.


ANCHOR STRINGS
==============

Each patch locates its insertion point by matching a short excerpt of the
upstream file, then asserts that the excerpt was found. Those excerpts are
quoted from the upstream sources listed above and are reproduced here only to
identify a position in a file.


